      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write an improved version of the test with better understandability — removing unused constants, adding clarifying comments, and making the flow easier to follow.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed unused constants (`TEXT_LATIN7`, `TEXT_LATIN15`, `TEXT_EUC_JP`, `TEXT_UNICODE`) that were leftover from the original larger test class, added Javadoc comments explaining the purpose of each helper method and the tricky `writerCheck` pattern, renamed `charset`/`writerCharset` to `expectedCharset`/`detectedCharset` for clarity, and grouped the three assertions with inline comments explaining what each one verifies."
